statement:
Let:
- m, P ∈ ℕ;
- μ a measure on the Borel sets of ℝ^P;
- M ⊆ ℝ^P Borel;
- for each j ∈ ℕ: C_j ⊆ ℝ^m compact, ψ_j : ℝ^m → ℝ^P continuous on C_j, and a predicate Good_j on ℝ^m.
Assume:
- μ(M ∖ ⋃_j ψ_j(C_j)) = 0;
- for every j, for μ⌞(M ∩ ψ_j(C_j))-a.e. x, every y ∈ C_j with ψ_j(y) = x satisfies Good_j(y).
Then there are Borel sets Y_j ⊆ C_j (j ∈ ℕ) such that:
- ψ_j(Y_j) ⊆ M;
- Good_j(y) holds for every y ∈ Y_j;
- the sets ψ_j(Y_j) are pairwise disjoint;
- μ(M ∖ ⋃_j ψ_j(Y_j)) = 0.
